WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.169 --> 00:00:05.779
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, thank you everyone
that submitted questions for this week’s

00:00:05.779 --> 00:00:06.779
Marvel Q&amp;A.

00:00:06.779 --> 00:00:08.910
This video is going to be a little extra special
just because some really big stuff is going

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:12.690
on in Hollywood and Robert Downey Jr just
happens to be at the center of it.

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:18.130
So there’s a bunch of cool stuff I wanted
to explain today.

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:23.020
The biggest news of the morning is that Robert
Downey Jr, in his own words, is going to ride

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:25.630
the Iron Man Wave into the shore.

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:28.210
So I’ll explain what that means before getting
to questions.

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:31.279
There are also a few announcements at the
end of the video.

00:00:31.279 --> 00:00:34.540
Just to start things off I want to ask everyone
a big question:

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:39.159
“How long is it okay for someone to play
a character?”

00:00:39.159 --> 00:00:41.030
Not just in the movies, just in general, animated,
anything anywhere.

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:45.609
There’s no real wrong answer to that, it’s
kind of an unfair question because characters

00:00:45.609 --> 00:01:01.319
change all the time, so 
Robert Downey Jr’s Iron Man in 2008 is a

00:01:01.319 --> 00:01:06.270
completely different person than the Iron
Man we’ll see in Avengers 2 next year.

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:13.740
Second point, the way we engage with them
over time changes a lot too.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:18.020
And when we get to watch people evolve with
their characters, it helps to keep us engaged.

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:27.710
Robert Downey Jr for all intents and purposes,
just said he’s going to keep being Iron

00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:31.710
Man until people stop buying tickets to Iron
Man movies.

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:32.710
Which is never.

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:35.380
How do I think this will play out?

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:42.000
First, as you may have already seen, he’s
using his superhero mega money and his super

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.369
fame to fund his own independent films like
The Judge.

00:01:44.369 --> 00:01:48.390
You’ll see a lot more of that.

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:53.060
It’s all done through his production company
Team Downey that he and his wife run.

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:59.850
The new model for actors in hollywood now
is to build an audience for themselves on

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:13.440
social media, whether it be facebook, instagram,
youtube and use that audience to develop their

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:16.230
own passion projects.

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:22.650
Some people start building the audience, then
break into hollywood, some do it in reverse.

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:23.980
Like Robert Downey Jr.

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:26.540
He just joined twitter a little while ago
and he even has a facebook page where he’s

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:27.540
been posting original videos.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:28.540
He’s using that to create awareness for
all these smaller projects he’s working

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:29.540
on.

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:34.550
Vin Diesel is another example of a big hollywood
actor that developed a large audience he shares

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:37.580
his passion projects with.

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:39.049
The last Riddick movie is a good example.

00:02:39.049 --> 00:02:40.049
He mortgaged his own house to fund part of
the movie.

00:02:40.049 --> 00:02:43.650
Without his facebook fandom, the movie would
have lost money and he would be homeless now.

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:45.349
It’s a really fascinating trend.

00:02:45.349 --> 00:02:52.660
So If you guys want me to talk more about
that kind of stuff just let me know.

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:55.840
Because it’s something that really fascinates
me from a creator perspective.

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:57.090
Now let’s answer some of your questions.

00:02:57.090 --> 00:03:01.890
I did include some movie stuff, but careful
for spoilers from episode 2 of shield...I’ll

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:06.370
wait just a sec...okay, here we go!

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:11.439
Question 1 - Alex asks, could Fitz be aware
he’s hallucinating Simmons and he’s just

00:03:11.439 --> 00:03:13.020
doing it to make himself feel better?

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:18.470
It seems like he knows that other people can’t
see her.

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:20.489
So something weird is going on.

00:03:20.489 --> 00:03:29.459
He seems crazy enough that he doesn’t think
he’s crazy to be talking to her.

00:03:29.459 --> 00:03:33.489
I think he’s completely at the point of
dissociation with reality that he just accepts

00:03:33.489 --> 00:03:36.610
head simmons is there as she exists in his
mind.

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:39.409
That’s why she’s always wearing the same
clothes from season 1.

00:03:39.409 --> 00:03:43.549
I don’t think he’s faking anything, I
think it’s an automatic defense mechanism

00:03:43.549 --> 00:03:54.269
his psyche conjured up to fill in gaps in
his brain’s normal ability to process information.

00:03:54.269 --> 00:03:59.590
Question 2 - J Moe asks, do you think the
blue TAHITI alien brought the obelisk to earth?

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:04.099
Yes, I also think the blue alien in the box
is the TAHITI alien.

00:04:04.099 --> 00:04:09.909
Like the one we saw in the tube being pumped
for the secret formula was the one they found

00:04:09.909 --> 00:04:11.519
in the crash in 1945.

00:04:11.519 --> 00:04:15.079
They’ve just kept some of it’s biological
systems alive so they can extract the genetic

00:04:15.079 --> 00:04:28.510
material they need.

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:32.050
Question 3 - Mike asks, Where is Isabelle
Hartley?

00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:34.730
We didn’t see her body in the casket?

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:42.570
They’re just leaving it open enough so they
can bring her back if they want.

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:50.090
Remember, Captain America and Nick Fury met
at his burial site.

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:53.090
Don’t assume that a funeral equals dead
forever.

00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:57.960
It’s not a guarantee we’ll see her again
this year, but Lucy Lawless said her contract

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:00.390
left all possibilities open.

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:05.700
Question 4 - Yami Jay asks, do you think Coulson
ordered Simmons to infiltrate HYDRA?

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:09.670
I don’t know about Coulson but I definitely
think someone ordered her to do it.

00:05:09.670 --> 00:05:13.650
She’s the shinning beacon of goodness on
the team, so I don’t think she’d be inside

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:15.970
HYDRA unless it was for a good reason.

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:20.690
It’s possible she took it on herself to
embed herself, she could be searching for

00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:26.720
something, like advanced technology or scientific
information.

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:41.480
Coulson knows everything apparently, so regardless
of why she’s there, he knows.

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:47.660
Question 5 - Aquaneos asks, do you think we’ll
ever get a Spider Woman reference on the show?

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:51.960
I think it’s a weird situation where Marvel
doesn’t have the rights to the spider man

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:54.310
charactes, but the do have the rights to Jessica
Drew and Spider Woman.

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:56.120
I think it has to do with her origins.

00:05:56.120 --> 00:06:00.660
There are a lot of legal rules about the use
of “Spider stuff” in marketing materials,

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:05.610
so if Marvel brought her on or referenced
her in some way it would probably be using

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:06.740
her real life name.

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:21.830
They’d say Agent Drew or Agent Jessica Drew.

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:27.130
Question 6 - xm 188 asks do you think they’ll
wait till the finale for skye to meet her

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:28.130
father?

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:33.610
No, I think it will happen before the mid-season
finale and during that episode they’ll activate

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:37.820
or try to use the obelisk in some way.

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:39.090
From a producer’s standpoint.

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:44.281
You want to end the season with a metaphorical
explosion, like a big Oh Shit moment, and

00:06:44.281 --> 00:06:47.140
leave people wondering what’s going to happen
after the big bang goes off.

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:51.740
It’s just a technique to keep people interested
until the show comes back.

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:55.640
I think the Agent Carter plot will overlap
with SHIELD this year.

00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:58.470
At least one of the stories will overlap with
the obelisk storyline, just because Agent

00:06:58.470 --> 00:07:06.120
Carter is going to air in SHIELD’s timeslot
while SHIELD is 

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:08.490
on break.

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:23.910
It’s just a powerful way for them to maintain
engagement and get SHIELD fans 

00:07:23.910 --> 00:07:38.140
to watch 
Agent Carter.

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:43.170
Question 7 - Tim asks how did Raina and the
Doctor touch the Obelisk without getting hurt?

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:47.730
I didn’t see Skye’s dad pick it up, but
I thought I heard him reference something

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:50.460
they did with it that changed what it looked
like.

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:51.970
The symbols weren’t quite as visible before
this final scene.

00:07:51.970 --> 00:07:52.970
So they did something to it.

00:07:52.970 --> 00:07:56.970
Based on what was said it sounds like the
object has a will of it’s own and allowed

00:07:56.970 --> 00:07:58.450
Raina to touch it.

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:03.730
I think that only certain meta humans will
be able to use it.

00:08:03.730 --> 00:08:10.900
Like Skye for instance.

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:18.210
Expect all of those things to be explained
in episodes which feature her dad.

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:22.760
Question 8 - Mariah asks what if the clockwork
orange device in the teaser for episode 3

00:08:22.760 --> 00:08:25.130
was used to ‘condition’ absorbing man?

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:26.130
Yes, definitely.

00:08:26.130 --> 00:08:33.690
I think Kraken uses that to brainwash SHIELD
agents into working for HYDRA and getting

00:08:33.690 --> 00:08:34.690
information.

00:08:34.690 --> 00:08:38.519
It’s just a way for them to control powerful
people.

00:08:38.519 --> 00:08:42.880
Don’t be surprised if one or more of the
big characters this season turn out to be

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:44.319
brainwashed.

00:08:44.319 --> 00:08:56.920
Like General Talbott.

00:08:56.920 --> 00:09:02.740
Question 9 - Bruno asks what if the third
faction is AIM?

00:09:02.740 --> 00:09:06.030
Baron Von Strucker did create AIM in the comics
after World War 2.

00:09:06.030 --> 00:09:08.829
I’d like to think it’s something new we
haven’t seen yet.

00:09:08.829 --> 00:09:10.410
I don’t need everything to be familiar.

00:09:10.410 --> 00:09:15.730
But SHIELD does typically draw from things
the movies have already set up.

00:09:15.730 --> 00:09:19.980
In the movies AIM wasn’t implied to be HYDRA,
Killian claimed he formed it himself.

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:22.050
And I don’t think he was HYDRA.

00:09:22.050 --> 00:09:30.800
So I’m thinking it’s something new.

